        <mxCell id="caption" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" value="Figure: Proposed POMA v3 inference pipeline. Stage 1 builds a structured query and three deterministic table views. Stage 2 runs three heterogeneous agents in parallel (a hint-routed text specialist, a program agent that executes pandas code locally, and a generalist on an alternate view) and canonicalizes their answers without an LLM. Stage 3 accepts agreement directly, sends disagreements to an execution-grounded adjudicator, and sends any Null prediction or Why question to a dedicated answerability agent, the only component allowed to output Null. Stage 4 formats a single final answer; thresholds and formatter rules are calibrated on the development split." vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="520" width="1390" height="70" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
